-- ============================================================================
-- 29: render-replica LIVE — the "effects missing/misplaced" OVER-EMIT is the
-- per-record sel==0xFF BLANK record. Diagnosed + fixed + validated 2026-06-14
-- from the prod ASMTRACE ground truth (PC 0x8C034864) coupled to a live replica-
-- live MCRR capture WITH 3 cat 1..4 projectiles firing every frame. NOT guessed.
-- Apply: tools/re_kb/rekb.sh @tools/re_kb/29_replica_effect_overemit_sel_ff.surql
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:asmtrace_efxdiag_295xxx SET kind='oracle_capture',
  ref='prod /dev/shm/mc_assembly.log (PC 0x8C034864, MAPLECAST_ASMTRACE=1, vframes 293997..296693) coupled to tools/render-replica-poc livecap MCRR (wss://nobd.net/replica-live, 2000 frames, vframes 295341..296481) + per-frame render_frame replay',
  note='Live coupled capture 2026-06-14. /dev/shm was 100%% full (tmpfs 2.0G) so the ASMTRACE log was FROZEN (gotcha from 23c); `cp /dev/null /dev/shm/mc_assembly.log` freed shm and the hook resumed writing fresh frames whose col-1 frame counter (0x8C3496B0) re-aligns with the livecap MCRR vframe. The matchup had 2 FIGHTER bodies (0c268340 P1C1 gfx1=0xc420040, 0c2688e4 P2C1 gfx1=0xc810040) + 3 cat 3/4 POOL-NODE projectiles every frame, ALL sharing the resident fighter GFX banks (gfx1=0xc420040, gfx2=0xc508680) and carrying body-range sels -> they render through the body GFX2 walker loc_8c0344d4. Across 1141 frames with engine ground truth, render_frame OVER-emitted (delta +1 or +4) on 254 frames; the 88-vs-84 case reproduced exactly at vframe 295515.';

UPSERT source:sel_ff_blank_record_disasm SET kind='marvelous2',
  ref='bank03.asm:10218 loc_8c0344d4 walker; record loop loc_8c03489e:10772; per-record entry loc_8c0345c4:10349 (@(0x6,r11)=sel); count gate loc_8c034782:10608 (cmp/pl); per-tile submit point loc_8c034864:10739',
  note='The body walker loc_8c0344d4 reads the GFX2 cell header u16 = record CAPACITY (NOT the live record count) at cellPtr, then walks `recCount` records. Each 8-byte record is [dx s16][dy s16][flags u16][sel u16@+6]. A record whose sel field == 0xFF is an authored BLANK/padding record: the engine emits ZERO visible tiles for it but STILL advances the per-tile descriptor cursor r13 (loc_8c034864 add 0x04,r13) and the per-record cursors past its slots, then CONTINUES to the next record. The trailing capacity records past the last real one are filler (sel=0, junk flags) and are likewise emitted as nothing. PINNED: GFX2 0x508680 sel 67 -> cellPtr 0x50a246 header u16=9 (block size entry[68]-entry[67]=74B=2+9*8 confirms 9-record CAPACITY); engine renders records 0..7 (sels 259,256,252,254,253,257,258,260 = 21 tiles) and emits 0 for record 8 (sel=0xFF, a VALID GFX1 selector with header (1,4,1,4) — so it is NOT an OOB/degenerate case, it is the authored blank sentinel).';

UPSERT source:sel_ff_overemit_validation SET kind='transpile_validation',
  ref='tools/render-replica-poc render_frame.{wasm,mjs} (md5 b0df15fd117226e6c269fdcf2200b234) replayed over the live MCRR + diffed vs the synced ASMTRACE slice',
  note='ROOT CAUSE pinned per-node: on the over-emit frames render_frame attributed +4 EXTRA quads to a BODY node (0c268340 vf295515: render_frame 25 tiles vs engine 21; the extra 4 = [255,255,255,255] = the rec-8 sel=0xFF blank record tiled by the un-guarded walker). The shared-gfx1-group cursor in _live_fidelity.mjs then mis-aligned, so the projectile nodes 0c26afc4/0c26adf4 read the previous node`s overflow quads -> apparent 133px/158px position errors = the "effects missing/misplaced" the user saw. FIX VALIDATED: across ALL 1141 ground-truth frames render_frame total quad count now == engine ASMTRACE part count (0 mismatch, down from 254); per-node engineParts==renderFrameQuads with max |dX|/|dY|=0.00px per node and global MAX |dX|=0.003px |dY|=0.004px (sub-pixel FP-contraction, well within the 0.5px gate). 487 node-frames in the capture carried a mid-stream sel==0xFF; all now handled. WRONG FIXES RULED OUT (traced, not guessed): (a) terminate-the-walk on sel==0xFF -> UNDER-emit -6 (wrongly dropped the valid records after the blank, e.g. 0c2688e4 vf295439 recs 13..16 sels 230,256,260,258); (b) force the record tile count to 0 in the walker -> froze r13 and phase-shifted later records by 1 tile each (256:2->1, 260:1->2, 258:2->1). The CORRECT model: the walker is left UNTOUCHED so every cursor advances exactly as the engine; only the VISIBLE quad capture is suppressed.';

UPSERT finding:replica_effect_overemit_sel_ff SET
  statement='CONFIRMED + FIXED 2026-06-14. The render-replica "not all effects are showing / effects misplaced" symptom was a per-frame OVER-EMIT (not a missing-render and NOT a read-set/residency gap). The body walker loc_8c0344d4 reads the GFX2 cell header as a record CAPACITY and walks all of it; a cell record whose sel field (@(r11+6)) == 0xFF is an authored BLANK record the engine renders as ZERO tiles (advancing cursors and continuing). The faithful transpile (gen_walker.c) tiled that blank record into stray quads (e.g. +4 [255,255,255,255]); because bodies + their projectiles/effects SHARE one gfx1 group and the client consumes that group in object order, the extra quads shifted every later quad in the group -> projectiles/effects drew at the wrong screen position (the user-visible misplacement). On THIS prod matchup every cat 1..4 node was a body-sprite projectile sharing a resident fighter GFX bank, so render_frame already DISPATCHED + positioned them (finding:replica_live_satellite_dispatch, 23c) — the bug was purely the shared-group cursor shift from the blank-record over-emit, present on 254 of 1141 frames (488 node-frames carry a mid-stream sel==0xFF). FIX (faithful, drift-free): in render_frame.c submit_1244b0, suppress the per-tile quad capture when its cell record sel (read at c->r[11]+6) == 0xFF; the walker is left UNTOUCHED so r13 and all cursors stay exactly in engine phase, so the records AFTER the blank render in-phase. gen_walker.c (the 0.00px-validated walker) is NOT edited. VALIDATED to count-exact + 0.00px-per-node across ALL 1141 ground-truth frames (source:sel_ff_overemit_validation). Rebuilt web/render-replica/render_frame.{wasm,mjs} (md5 b0df15fd117226e6c269fdcf2200b234, web==node byte-identical); deployed surgically to prod /var/www/maplecast/render-replica (md5-verified) with replay.html render_frame cache-bust ?v=selff1 (other modules left untouched). NOTE: PURE effects in the Effect-Poly bank 0x0CED0000 and satellites whose GFX is NOT a resident fighter bank were NOT present in this capture (every cat 1..4 node shared gfx1=0xc420040/gfx2=0xc508680); those remain the OPEN static-once-GFX residency class (finding:replica_live_static_gfx_gap covers bodies; collectFreshGfx + buildTables in maplecast_replica_live.cpp gate on cat==0, so a non-resident satellite/effect GFX is still shipped only from the frozen connect seed — to be exercised when a matchup fires one). Branch feat/render-replica-live.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:replica_effect_overemit_sel_ff->cites->source:asmtrace_efxdiag_295xxx;
RELATE finding:replica_effect_overemit_sel_ff->cites->source:sel_ff_blank_record_disasm;
RELATE finding:replica_effect_overemit_sel_ff->cites->source:sel_ff_overemit_validation;
RELATE finding:replica_effect_overemit_sel_ff->cites->routine:loc_8c0344d4;
RELATE finding:replica_effect_overemit_sel_ff->about->finding:replica_live_satellite_dispatch;

-- ---- OPEN sub-item: non-resident satellite/effect GFX residency (the read-set cat-0 gate) ----
UPSERT finding:replica_live_satellite_gfx_residency SET
  statement='OPEN (raised 2026-06-14, not yet triggered). maplecast_replica_live.cpp ships fresh GFX1/GFX2 ONLY for cat==0 BODY nodes: buildTables (the L-loop `if (rd8(node+0x3)!=0) continue`) and collectFreshGfx (`if (rd8(node+0x3)!=0) continue`) both skip cat 1..4. A satellite/effect whose GFX is its OWN region (not a resident fighter bank) or the shared Effect-Poly bank 0x0CED0000 therefore reads its cell records ONLY from the frozen connect-time 16MB ram16 seed; if that art loads/changes AFTER connect (a super, a character-specific projectile, a hitspark type not resident at connect), the walker reads stale cell records -> wrong tile count / garbage -> that effect missing or misplaced. This is the cat!=0 twin of finding:replica_live_static_gfx_gap (which fixed it for bodies). NOT reproduced on the 2026-06-14 capture (1500+ live frames probed: ZERO cat 1..4 nodes used the Effect-Poly bank or a non-resident GFX2 — every satellite shared gfx1=0xc420040/gfx2=0xc508680, a resident fighter bank). FIX WHEN TRIGGERED: extend collectFreshGfx (and buildTables) to ALSO walk cat 1..4 nodes` GFX1/GFX2, OR ship the Effect-Poly bank 0x0CED0000 as an on-change dynamic region. Requires a contact-frame capture with a non-resident-GFX effect on screen to validate.',
  status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:replica_live_satellite_gfx_residency->about->finding:replica_live_static_gfx_gap;
RELATE finding:replica_live_satellite_gfx_residency->cites->source:replica_live_cpp;
